.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-admin-wallets - Any account's wallets: list them, see what names one, switch it off or on (lists when run bare)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 admin wallets [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the wallets of an account (--account), each with the tokens it accepts and, when
it is off, who switched it off (deactivated_by: owner or operator).

.PP
The account is always named with --account: 'rail0 admin accounts --search 0x…' finds
the account a wallet address belongs to.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--account\fP=""
	The account the wallets belong to (required)

.PP
\fB--active\fP=""
	Only wallets that are on ('true') or off ('false')

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for wallets

.PP
\fB--page\fP=0
	Page number (1-based)

.PP
\fB--per-page\fP=0
	Wallets per page

.PP
\fB--sort\fP=""
	Sort wallets (e.g. -created_at)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 admin wallets --account 019e748b-…
  rail0 admin wallets --account 019e748b-… --active false --pretty
  rail0 admin wallets usage 0x2D2B… --account 019e748b-…
  rail0 admin wallets deactivate 0x2D2B… --account 019e748b-…
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-admin(1)\fP, \fBrail0-admin-wallets-activate(1)\fP, \fBrail0-admin-wallets-deactivate(1)\fP, \fBrail0-admin-wallets-usage(1)\fP
